{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8f3c1e2a-5d47-4b19-9a6e-7c2f10b4d3e5",
    "name": "LCC Student Portal · Do It Online Forms (App API)",
    "description": "The eight \"Do it online\" forms the College now takes in-house, as endpoints for the React Native app.\n\n**One pair per form.** `GET` hands over what the app cannot know - the student's own record and the lists it has to choose from. `POST` takes the filled-in form, saves the row, raises a Service Desk ticket in Operations and emails the student a receipt. There is no form builder: build the screens with native inputs and post the field names below.\n\n**Auth.** Every endpoint sits behind the `student-api` bearer guard. Run *Auth → Login* first; it writes the token into the `access_token` collection variable and the rest of the requests pick it up.\n\n**Dates** go out and come back as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n**Bodies** are `multipart/form-data` so that uploads and repeating blocks work the same way everywhere. Repeating blocks are indexed (`assignments[0][title]`); multi-selects repeat the key (`reasons[]`).\n\n**Responses.** Success is `201` with `{ success: true, data: { id, reference, status, submitted_at, message } }`. `status` is `raised` when the ticket exists, or `queued` when Operations could not be reached - the submission is safe either way and a retry job finishes it, so treat `queued` as success and show the student the message from the response.\n\n**Validation** failures are `422` with `{ success: false, message, errors: { field: [...] } }`, keyed by the field names in these requests (nested rows come back as `absences.0.absent_to`). The messages are written for students and can be shown as they are.\n\n**Uploads** are optional on most forms, capped at 5 files of 5MB (10MB on form 9), pdf/doc/docx/jpg/jpeg/png. On forms 4, 8 and 16 at least one file is required when `evidence_method=upload`.\n\nEvery GET returns the same `student` block - `id`, `full_name`, `name`, `student_id`, `email`, `mobile`, `address`, `course`, `course_start_date`, `intake` - so the app can show the details box without a second call. The lists each GET returns (courses, reasons, grounds, issue types) are the only values the matching POST will accept, so build the pickers from them rather than hard-coding labels.\n\nThe four `device_*` fields are optional everywhere and are only recorded against the submission for support.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "https://lcc_datafuture.test",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "No trailing slash. Live: https://portal.lcc.ac.uk"
    },
    {
      "key": "access_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Filled in by Auth -> Login."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "description": "Run this first. The token it returns is stored in `access_token` and used by every other request.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const token = body.token || body.access_token || (body.data && (body.data.token || body.data.access_token));",
                  "if (token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('access_token', token);",
                  "    console.log('access_token stored');",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.warn('No token in the login response - set access_token by hand.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "email",
                  "value": "student@example.com",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "The student's portal email address."
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "password",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "The student's portal password."
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/login",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The portal's existing student login. Returns the Passport bearer token the form endpoints need."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "9 · Course Change Request",
